From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:49:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thunderbolt: apple: Add the T8132 LSTX GPIO

The T8132 routers take their LSTX sideband pin from the AOP pin
controller once they are up. Describe that pin as a GPIO too, so the
host can hold the line once a router has stopped, and document the
"lstx" pinctrl state that hands the pin to the router.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit f017e3df4b2c968abdf07735ecbe067e29ee8f4c)
---
 .../bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml   | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
index 90717301e2..434a833cd3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
@@ -83,6 +83,11 @@ properties:
       Marks this root complex as the USB4/Thunderbolt switch that the Type-C
       PD controller hands cable information to, so the Type-C mux can find it.
 
+  lstx-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      GPIO on the pin that carries the router's LSTX sideband signal.
+
   apple,pcie-tunnel:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
@@ -193,6 +198,12 @@ allOf:
           minItems: 4
         reg-names:
           minItems: 4
+        pinctrl-names:
+          items:
+            - const: lstx
+    else:
+      properties:
+        lstx-gpios: false
 
 additionalProperties: false
 
